# MEDTRACK DV – KPI CALCULATIONS
## MILESTONE 2 – KPI ENGINEERING & DASHBOARD PLANNING

This document contains the KPI calculations and Tableau calculated fields used in the MedTrack DV – Hospital Operations & Patient Analytics Dashboard.

---

# 1. TOTAL ADMISSIONS

## Calculated Field Name
Total Admissions

## Tableau Formula

COUNT([Patient ID])

## Description
Counts the total number of patient admission records available in the dataset.

## Purpose
- Measures hospital patient volume.
- Monitors admission workload.
- Supports hospital capacity planning.

## Visualization
KPI Card

---

# 2. AVERAGE LENGTH OF STAY (ALOS)

## Calculated Field Name
Average Length of Stay

## Tableau Formula

AVG([Length of Stay])

## Alternative Formula

If the dataset column is named `Length of Stay (days)`:

AVG([Length of Stay (days)])

## Description
Calculates the average number of days patients stay in the hospital.

## Purpose
- Measures treatment efficiency.
- Helps analyze patient flow.
- Supports bed management.

## Visualization
KPI Card and Bar Chart

---

# 3. READMITTED PATIENTS

## Calculated Field Name
Readmitted Patients

## Tableau Formula

SUM(
    IF [Re-admission Flag] = "Yes"
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0
    END
)

## Description
Counts the number of patients whose Re-admission Flag is marked as "Yes".

## Purpose
- Identifies readmitted patients.
- Supports readmission analysis.
- Helps evaluate patient care outcomes.

---

# 4. READMISSION RATE

## Calculated Field Name
Readmission Rate

## Tableau Formula

SUM(
    IF [Re-admission Flag] = "Yes"
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0
    END
)
/
COUNT([Patient ID])

## Format

Format the calculated field as Percentage.

## Description
Measures the proportion of patients who were marked as readmitted.

## Purpose
- Monitors readmission patterns.
- Supports healthcare quality analysis.
- Helps identify potential patient-care issues.

## Visualization
KPI Card and Line Chart

---

# 5. OCCUPIED PATIENTS

## Calculated Field Name
Occupied Patients

## Tableau Formula

SUM(
    IF [Bed Status] = "Occupied"
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0
    END
)

## Description
Counts patient records where the Bed Status is "Occupied".

## Purpose
- Analyzes occupied patient records.
- Supports ward-level resource analysis.
- Helps understand bed-status distribution.

## Visualization
KPI Card and Bar Chart

---

# 6. OCCUPANCY RATE

## Important Dataset Note

A true hospital occupancy rate requires reliable total-bed-capacity information.

## Formula

SUM(
    IF [Bed Status] = "Occupied"
    THEN 1
    ELSE 0
    END
)
/
SUM([Total Beds])

## Format

Format as Percentage.

## Important

If the dataset does NOT contain a `Total Beds` field, this calculation should not be presented as a true hospital occupancy rate.

Instead, use:

Occupied Patients

or:

Bed Utilization by Ward

This avoids creating an unsupported denominator.

